--- !u!114 &255896631
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 255896630}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ff7b1b1a1ce50e438b5e732152d10e8, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCInteraction
  conversation:
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: Custodian. The <color=#FFB300>USC Wayfarer</color> missed its standard
      orbital check-in. It is currently experiencing a localized comms blackout.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Uh... right. The Wayfarer. Wait, is that one of the big deep-space
      freighters? I usually just clean the lunar transit hubs.
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: Your previous assignments are irrelevant. It is a Class-A hauler,
      and Aether-Core is not authorizing the budget for a rescue tug. You are cheaper
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Hey, I just scrub filters and mop decks. What am I supposed to
      do about a blackout on a Class-A?
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: You will dock your craft, walk to the server room, and perform
      a manual reset on the router. It is unskilled labor."
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: What about the crew? Don't those haulers have, like, a whole team
      on board? Can't one of them just flip the switch?
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: There is a biological monitoring crew of exactly fifty personnel.
      They are likely locked out of the mainframe due to a routine fault
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Fifty people are locked out of their own ship, and you're sending
      a Junior Custodian?
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: Do not question me, Kaelen. Your job is to reboot the system and
      wait for them to buy you a drink.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Right. Okay. And my gear? Am I getting hazard pay? A security escort?
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: You are receiving something far more valuable. You have been temporarily
      issued an Aether-Core <color=#FFB300>M.E.T. Rig</color>.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: A what? It looks like a heavy diving suit glued to a server rack.
      The cooling fans are deafening.
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: It is a Matter Engram Translator. It uses Quantum-Enthalpy Digitization
      to store physical matter as data.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Speak English, please. I make nine credits an hour.
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: It means you can carry heavy objects in a digital inventory. It
      is a multi-million credit piece of proprietary hardware.
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: Let me be absolutely clear, Custodian. The <color=#FFB300>M.E.T.
      Rig</color> is worth exponentially more than your life insurance payout.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: Wait, what? Are you saying if I die out there...
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: If you encounter a catastrophic hazard, protocol dictates you shield
      the Rig with your body to prevent hardware damage.
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: Get in. Do not scratch the <color=#FFB300>M.E.T. Rig</color>. Reboot
      the system, and do not fail us.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: ...
  firedConversation:
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: You want me to walk onto a Class-A derelict with a fifty-man dead
      crew? No. I quit. Keep your nine credits an hour
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: "You misunderstand the nature of your contract, Custodian. Aether-Core
      owns the oxygen scrubbers in your transit hub.\t"
  - speakerName: DIRECTOR OF ORBITAL LOGISTICS
    dialogueText: Your employment is terminated. Security will escort you to the
      airlock. Do not expect a severance package.
  - speakerName: SYSTEM
    dialogueText: <color=#E63946>SYSTEM ARCHIVE // EMPLOYEE 8449-K TERMINATED. LOCKING
      HUB DOORS.
  interactionPrompt: {fileID: 1249728530}
  dialogueEngine: {fileID: 1441849084}
  gameOverScreen: {fileID: 847422448}
